From 2953c7155d9b9aa058437986b785882b0193fa45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikael Hug <mikaelhug@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:16:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: apple: Set driver data before the first cable
 connect

dwc3_apple_remove() takes the glue state from the platform driver data,
but only dwc3_core_probe() sets it, and that runs lazily on the first
role switch to host or device. Unbinding the driver (or unloading the
module) before any USB cable was connected therefore dereferences NULL
when it takes appledwc->lock.

Set the driver data to the embedded struct dwc3 in probe, the same
pointer dwc3_core_probe() stores later, so remove works in every state.

Found while tracing the role flow on the Mac mini (M2, j473): port 1
(Back-right) stays in DWC3_APPLE_PROBE_PENDING until a USB partner
appears, so its drvdata is NULL for the whole boot without a cable.

Fixes: 0ec946d32ef7 ("usb: dwc3: Add Apple Silicon DWC3 glue layer driver")

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UqitcmCNS6G33aQUShi39x
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
index 40c3ccfddb67..44bca0e9cc0f 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
@@ -475,6 +475,7 @@ static int dwc3_apple_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	 * details.
 	 */
 	appledwc->state = DWC3_APPLE_PROBE_PENDING;
+	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, &appledwc->dwc);
 	ret = dwc3_apple_setup_role_switch(appledwc);
 	if (ret)
 		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, ret, "Failed to setup role switch\n");
